Name: quic_ebpf_iface
Type: STRING
Default-Value: NULL
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

Whitespace-separated list of network interfaces to attach the QUIC
eBPF connection-ID steering program to (e.g. "eth0 wlan0"). Only
consulted when a proto="quic" service is configured in cyrus.conf, and
only when this build was compiled with eBPF support and
:option:`quic_ebpf` hasn't disabled it; ignored otherwise.

If unset (the default), the program is instead attached to every
network interface this host currently has, discovered automatically
at startup -- an interface that fails to attach (unusual/virtual,
down, ...) is logged and skipped rather than treated as fatal. Set
this explicitly to attach to only a specific subset of interfaces
instead; in that case every named interface must attach successfully,
or master fails to start, since a typo or a genuinely broken interface
here should be loud immediately rather than silently leaving HTTP/3
unreachable on just that one network.

See master/quic/quic_ebpf.c for what this program does and why it's
needed: it lets each QUIC connection be dispatched to its own worker
process, the same way TCP's accept() does, despite QUIC having no
equivalent of accept() at the socket layer.
